// Level 2: The Rail Yard (working name), a disused goods yard and engine shed.
// World frame: metres, x east, z south (north is −Z), y up. A brick wall encloses x −75…75, z −40…40; you come in at
// the south gate, the breach in the east wall or the gap in the west wall.
// Four tracks run east–west the length of the yard (z −24, −17, −8, −1), the first two on into the engine shed in the
// north-west and the fourth through the goods shed; rakes of derelict wagons stand on them with gaps between, so the
// lanes along the tracks are long and the crossings short and exposed. The footbridge crosses them all at x 0.
// Perimeter wall segments: 0 north (x −75→75, at_m = x + 75), 1 east (z −40→40, at_m = z + 40),
// 2 south (x 75→−75, at_m = 75 − x), 3 west (z 40→−40, at_m = 40 − z).
